  9487	  5. **D431's "same day," for a run longer than one day.** A new-system draw takes about 20 h, so one calendar day cannot hold it.
  9488	     - The six counted draws are launched within one hour of each other and run concurrently.
  9489	     - A redo within a draw counts as part of that draw.
  9490	     - Every counted send falls within 72 h of the first launch.
  9491	     - A breach makes the result a diagnostic.
  9492	     - This replaces, for this run only, the one-calendar-day reading in `WIRING-DESIGN.md`.
  9493	  6. **No replacement draw counts.** A draw that cannot finish gives no release verdict; what finished goes to Alex as a diagnostic. The
  9494	     reviewers read "same day" differently, so the council took the cheaper, reversible course (D439).
  9495	  7. **The credit and scoring rules** are plan §1.4:
