The native-ID sampler, redo selection, mapping validation, prior-round debate, publisher lookup and independently confirmed plants are fixed. I accept D675’s frozen-rule readings. Independent prompts receive neither the key nor peer marks. I checked publishers on both historical stores and left the live outputs unopened. [D675](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9690) · [Sampler and plants](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py:88) · [Reader prompts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py:227)

- **Eligibility still checks the wrong evidence.** It accepts a matching draw label without verifying the recorded run options or September 20 cutoff. It also checks the latest archived response timestamp. Failed transport attempts can be charged without creating an archive row. Verify the registered run options and use complete attempt records to establish D667’s timing. [Eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:43) · [Archive writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:260) · [Attempt ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:272) · [D667](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9487)
- **The verdict still trusts unverified fingerprints.** I reproduced a practical lead with 20 synthetic matters, the real matter-file hash and placeholder fingerprints for everything else. Compare the scored matter rows with the frozen list and verify the eligibility, mapping and deck fingerprints against the artifacts actually used. [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:153) · [Test fixture](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:16)
- **The split report still loses disagreements.** I reproduced an empty split report when one question clearly covered one matter and had split coverage on another. Report coverage splits from each matter-question pair. Keep the card-level flag for guardrail inclusion. [Deck](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py:130) · [Report](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:134)
- **Cards hide the opening order needed to judge duplicates.** They list other questions in order but omit where the card’s own question sits. Mark which questions opened earlier using the stored order, including same-day openings. [Renderer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_cards.py:86) · [Duplicate rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md:143)

NOT READY: verify run eligibility and scorer inputs, report every mapping split, and show which questions opened earlier.
